/-!
# Genuine Appell--Humbert automorphy and entire theta-function obstructions

For the actual full period lattices, the explicit Appell--Humbert
transformation law with norm-one multiplier implies that the weighted
norm is continuous and periodic, hence globally bounded. The Hermitian
form of a nonzero entire theta function is therefore positive
semidefinite. For the zero Hermitian form, the theta function is constant;
if it is nonzero, its multiplier is identically one.

Combined with the independently proved intrinsic type-`(1,1)`
classification, these conclusions force every nonzero theta function
for an integral alternating form outside the countable exceptional
locus to be a nonzero constant for the zero form.

The transformation law is an explicit hypothesis on actual entire
functions. These files do not assume or assert an Appell--Humbert
classification of arbitrary line bundles, a presentation theorem for
their sections, or an algebraic-dimension conclusion.
-/
